 We are seeking a Tax Advisor to join our team of tax professionals and provide tax advisory services to our Canadian and U.S. entities, as well as to the various business lines across iA Financial Group. The successful candidate will also contribute to strategic tax planning aimed at optimizing the Group’s tax efficiency and achieving corporate objectives while ensuring compliance with applicable laws and regulations.
 What you’ll accomplish with us 
As a Tax Advisor, Canadian Corporate Tax and Advisory Services you’ll be at the core of our mission. 
 Here are the main responsibilities:
 Providing tax advisory services to the Group’s entities and business lines, particularly with respect to corporate taxation and the taxation of insurance and retirement products;
 Conducting complex tax research requiring extensive and in-depth knowledge in your area of expertise, preparing tax opinions and delivering recommendations;
 Acting as a subject matter expert on special mandates, business acquisition projects and corporate reorganizations;
 Providing support to managers, business units and Group entities on corporate and product taxation matters;
 Participating in and providing the required support for the tax compliance process across iA Financial Group entities;
 Participating in and representing iA Financial Group during audits conducted by tax authorities and external auditors within your area of expertise;
 Monitoring legislative and regulatory developments to ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulations and advising management of the potential impacts of changes;
 Advancing and evolving organizational practices within your area of expertise in collaboration with various teams across the Executive Vice-Presidency and other stakeholders;
 Participating in various committees, working groups and other relevant forums as a representative of your area of expertise;
 Actively contributing to the development, implementation and optimization of the team’s processes, procedures and standards within your area of expertise.
 What could accelerate your success in this role 
We’re looking for someone who: 
 Holds a bachelor’s degree in business administration or accounting ;
 Holds a master’s degree in taxation or has completed the CPA Canada In-Depth Tax Program ;
 Has at least four years of relevant experience in Canadian corporate taxation; relevant cross-border tax experience is considered an asset ;
 Holds a CPA designation, an asset ;
 Is recognized for their strong analytical and synthesis skills ;
 Has experience with CCH IntelliConnect or Taxnet Pro ;
 Is fluent in French and has an intermediate level of proficiency in English, as the role requires weekly communication with internal and external clients located across Canada.
 Why you’ll love working with us 
 A work environment where learning and development merge with a collective pursuit of excellence;
 A healthy, safe, fair, and inclusive environment where potential can be freely expressed and developed;
 The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment, supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces;
 Competitive benefits : Flexible group insurance, competitive pension plan, stock purchase plan, vacation and wellness/personal development days, telemedicine, employee and family assistance program, ergonomic furniture program, performance bonus, discounts on iA products, and much more!
 Apply now and get ahead of your career, where your talent really belongs!  
 Still unsure about applying? 
At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, go ahead and apply – your place might be with us, and we want to get to know you! 
